<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#DataType> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A reusable declaration of how a primitive field value is represented and interpreted, including its base category, width, signedness and optional RDF datatype."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#DataType> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use in physical binary-format descriptions. Extents and offsets describe bytes unless a term explicitly specifies bits; HEL evaluation and failure behavior follow the processing specification. Assert this class on a resource representing the defined entity; subclass links below are the asserted hierarchy, not merely similarity links."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#DataTypeOrStruct> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The union of a primitive datatype declaration and a structured record declaration; either can supply a field's effective type."@en .
